WEBVTT

00:12.150 --> 00:14.820
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

00:15.660 --> 00:19.030
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
Super Cute Angels ♥

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Boom!</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Super Adorable</b>

01:30.690 --> 01:35.440
<b>Episode 12:
Life Without You Feels Super Off</b>

01:30.690 --> 01:35.440
<b>Episode 12:
Life Without You Feels Super Off</b>

01:46.760 --> 01:49.710
Excuse me, but the park is about to close.

01:50.810 --> 01:54.620
Oh that's right! If we don't hurry, 
we'll miss the bus home!

01:54.620 --> 01:57.210
You're right! Let's hurry, Fuyuki-san!

01:57.210 --> 02:01.530
Oh. Um, today's final bus has already left.

02:01.530 --> 02:02.220
Huh?!

02:02.220 --> 02:04.770
But there's still one scheduled for...

02:04.770 --> 02:08.040
Yeah, you're probably looking 
at the weekday schedule.

02:08.520 --> 02:13.500
On weekends and holidays, the number of 
trips and departure times are very different.

02:15.900 --> 02:19.150
A-All right. I'll try calling my dad.

02:19.150 --> 02:21.660
Okay. I'll call my mom, too.

02:21.890 --> 02:23.620
<b>Tsubasa
Incoming Call</b>

02:22.810 --> 02:23.620
Hmm?

02:25.050 --> 02:26.950
Hey. What's up, Tsubasa?

02:26.950 --> 02:28.360
Hello. Dad?

02:28.360 --> 02:33.110
Um, I'm with a friend in this 
place called Higashimokoto.

02:33.110 --> 02:34.590
<i>Shibazakura Park?</i>

02:34.590 --> 02:41.720
<b>Kitami
Station</b>

02:34.590 --> 02:41.720
<b>Higashimokoto Shibazakura Park</b>

02:35.610 --> 02:37.630
Oh? I see, I see.

02:37.630 --> 02:41.730
<i>It's only about an hour by car 
from Kitami to Higashimokoto.</i>

02:42.100 --> 02:44.840
<i>Well, if anything happens 
I can just go pick him up.</i>

02:45.340 --> 02:48.540
Tsubasa, do you want to spend 
more time with your friend?

02:48.540 --> 02:51.440
<i>Huh?! Uh... Mm-hmm.</i>

02:51.440 --> 02:53.730
Okay! In that case...

02:53.730 --> 02:55.940
Whaaat?!

02:55.940 --> 02:57.840
But, Dad, that's...!

02:57.840 --> 02:59.390
Um, hello?!

02:59.390 --> 03:01.540
Wh-What's wrong, Tsubasa?

03:02.590 --> 03:04.200
Uh, well,

03:04.200 --> 03:09.790
my dad says he has a friend who works at a 
hotel here, so he wants us to stay there.

03:09.790 --> 03:11.790
S-Seriously?

03:13.970 --> 03:19.060
<i>Dad... he must have gotten the wrong idea 
and thought I was with a guy friend.</i>

03:19.060 --> 03:21.010
<i>What do I do now?</i>

03:21.500 --> 03:23.070
That reminds me.

03:24.520 --> 03:27.740
Remember when we all went out for yakiniku?

03:27.740 --> 03:30.600
On the way home, we talked about 
having a sleep-over date sometime.

03:31.640 --> 03:33.770
I guess it's actually happening.

03:34.970 --> 03:39.630
B-But is this okay? 
Spending the night all of a sudden...

03:39.630 --> 03:41.780
Aren't your parents worried?

03:44.600 --> 03:45.700
It's okay.

03:46.570 --> 03:48.620
I already told Mom about it.

03:51.150 --> 03:53.860
Oh, right. We haven't had dinner yet.

03:53.860 --> 03:55.770
We should go before the restaurants close.

03:55.770 --> 03:56.420
Yeah!

03:57.210 --> 03:59.570
Mom! Where's Big Mii?

03:59.570 --> 04:03.900
Your sister said she's sleeping 
over at a friend's house.

04:03.900 --> 04:07.800
Huh? No fair! I want to sleep over, too!

04:07.800 --> 04:09.600
You're staying right here.

04:09.600 --> 04:11.450
Aww!

04:13.910 --> 04:17.190
Kids sure grow up fast.

04:18.010 --> 04:20.320
Wow! Awesome!

04:20.320 --> 04:22.470
Yeah, this looks really good!

04:22.470 --> 04:25.070
I have to thank your father for this.

04:25.070 --> 04:26.010
Yeah!

04:26.010 --> 04:28.680
<i>Dad, thanks a whole lot!</i>

04:29.560 --> 04:32.360
Mmm! It's so good!

04:32.830 --> 04:34.870
Oh! Hey, that one's mine!

04:34.870 --> 04:36.430
Mmm!

04:36.430 --> 04:38.790
Aww, Fuyuki-san!

04:39.430 --> 04:41.890
Whew! I'm so stuffed!

04:41.890 --> 04:45.150
Yeah. Me, too. I guess we 
should go back to the room.

04:45.150 --> 04:46.140
Yeah.

04:46.670 --> 04:51.390
<i>Easier said than done. 
What are we supposed to do after that?</i>

04:51.390 --> 04:53.710
I'll be in a room alone with Fuyuki-san!

04:54.490 --> 04:58.900
Hey, Tsubasa. When we get back, 
is it okay if I take a shower first?

04:58.900 --> 05:00.300
<i>Huh?!</i>

05:04.150 --> 05:07.820
<i>Th-Th-This is bad! 
What am I gonna d-d-do?!</i>

05:08.130 --> 05:10.280
<i>Get a hold of yourself, man!</i>

05:26.650 --> 05:27.550
Tsubasa.

05:34.470 --> 05:35.530
Fuyuki-san.

05:43.240 --> 05:47.020
<i>No, no, no, no, what the hell am I thinking?!</i>

05:47.020 --> 05:51.200
<i>Oh, right. That's right. 
The same thing happened before,</i>

05:51.200 --> 05:54.270
<i>and it was always just me 
getting the wrong idea.</i>

05:54.270 --> 05:58.590
<i>Yeah, there's no way Fuyuki-san would 
be thinking about something like that!</i>

06:04.670 --> 06:06.070
<b>Fields of Moss Phlox at Higashimokoto Park</b>

06:04.670 --> 06:06.070
<b>When Can You See Them? And for How Long?</b>

06:04.670 --> 06:07.420
<b>Muted</b>

06:05.000 --> 06:05.810
Oh.

06:06.070 --> 06:07.420
<b>Shibazakura Soft Serve</b>

06:06.070 --> 06:07.420
<b>A Flavor That Memories Are Made Of</b>

06:13.770 --> 06:18.980
<i>I wonder... if I'll ever 
see Fuyuki-san again.</i>

06:39.270 --> 06:40.350
Okay.

06:43.940 --> 06:46.550
Tsubasa, you're up.

06:56.570 --> 06:58.940
Okay. You fell asleep.

07:00.020 --> 07:02.600
I'm not surprised. You must be exhausted.

07:08.420 --> 07:09.550
Tsubasa...

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Tamu-san's Page

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Profile

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Friend List

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Recommendations

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Friend Requests

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
User Settings

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Hanekoto

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Last Played  10 Days Ago

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Gaming History

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
All Together! Monster Climbing

07:36.810 --> 07:41.810
Played for over 10 Hours

07:37.110 --> 07:41.810
<i>He didn't log in at all during break 
and when I text he doesn't answer.</i>

07:42.230 --> 07:44.050
<i>I wonder if something happened to him.</i>

07:44.050 --> 07:46.270
Oh? Is that Sayu-nee?

07:47.220 --> 07:48.230
Asuka?

07:48.230 --> 07:51.450
I never see you out and about this early.

07:52.650 --> 07:55.110
And you're just playing games again.

07:55.860 --> 07:58.120
Oh, shut up! So what if I am?

07:58.120 --> 07:59.540
It's cool.

08:00.190 --> 08:03.750
Oh, Hina. Old friend of mine. 
She's a year ahead. Sayu-nee.

08:04.230 --> 08:05.560
Pleased to meet you.

08:05.560 --> 08:06.630
I'm Akino.

08:07.710 --> 08:09.510
Oh, right! Sayu-nee,

08:09.510 --> 08:12.980
Hina and I are going to karaoke 
after. Do you want to come?

08:12.980 --> 08:13.870
Not a chance.

08:13.870 --> 08:15.750
Huh? Then how about a movie?

08:15.750 --> 08:17.480
There's nothing I want to see right now.

08:18.780 --> 08:21.790
Oh, come on! Weren't you gonna 
hang out with Hina-chan?

08:21.790 --> 08:25.140
Yeah but, Sayu-nee, we should hang out more!

08:25.140 --> 08:27.980
You're never gonna get a boyfriend 
playing games all the time.

08:27.980 --> 08:29.070
What?

08:29.350 --> 08:32.610
Akino-senpai, is there 
somebody that you like?

08:33.960 --> 08:36.330
No, not really.

08:36.330 --> 08:41.350
Whoa! There is, right? 
So who is it? Someone in your class?

08:42.280 --> 08:46.250
Drop it! I mean, why are 
we even talking about this?

08:45.220 --> 08:47.480
Calm down, you two.

08:48.870 --> 08:49.900
Welcome.

08:51.090 --> 08:51.880
Oh?

08:52.690 --> 08:53.970
It's Fuyuki-senpai.

08:54.220 --> 08:54.920
Huh?

08:57.930 --> 08:59.140
Coming!

09:00.190 --> 09:01.390
Good afternoon.

09:01.390 --> 09:03.010
Oh, hello.

09:03.010 --> 09:06.560
I made far too many of these, 
so I thought I might share.

09:06.860 --> 09:08.810
Oh! Kashiwa mochi?

09:09.280 --> 09:12.430
That's right. Today is Children's Day.

09:14.120 --> 09:16.540
Oh, did you want to see Tsubasa?

09:16.540 --> 09:18.220
He's in his room. Want me to get him?

09:18.220 --> 09:20.070
Oh, it's all right.

09:20.070 --> 09:25.540
I didn't see him much during the holiday, 
so I thought he might have taken ill.

09:25.540 --> 09:30.360
Hmm. Well, I don't think 
that's exactly the problem.

09:31.640 --> 09:34.650
I'm sorry you came over for nothing, though.

09:34.650 --> 09:37.300
Oh, not at all. Well then, goodbye.

09:37.300 --> 09:39.960
Bye! And thanks for the kashiwa mochi!

09:45.540 --> 09:49.410
What? You didn't even tell 
him about studying abroad?

09:49.410 --> 09:51.100
N-No.

09:52.820 --> 09:57.110
Oh, but then when we went 
out together, I did.

09:57.420 --> 09:58.280
Huh?!

10:00.740 --> 10:03.790
I guess Fuyuki-senpai is 
leaving to study abroad.

10:03.790 --> 10:05.540
Sounds like it.

10:05.540 --> 10:07.580
Oh, right...

10:07.580 --> 10:12.790
You're a Fuyuki-senpai fan because she 
reminds you of that character you like, right?

10:12.790 --> 10:13.670
Yeah.

10:18.260 --> 10:19.880
Thanks, Sayurin.

10:19.880 --> 10:20.790
Huh?

10:20.790 --> 10:24.200
For the advice you gave me before. 
I really appreciated it!

10:24.200 --> 10:25.830
Sure.

10:26.750 --> 10:31.390
Honestly, I was kind of surprised because 
you're always doing crazy stuff.

10:31.390 --> 10:33.720
I thought I'd mostly gotten used to it,

10:34.200 --> 10:36.490
but then all of a sudden you're 
talking about studying abroad?

10:37.420 --> 10:38.360
That wasn't a compliment.

10:38.670 --> 10:39.460
Yeah.

10:39.970 --> 10:45.800
But you know, I didn't want to wait. I 
thought if I didn't go now, I never would.

10:46.340 --> 10:49.710
You know me. I have so much fun every day!

10:49.710 --> 10:54.460
Going to school, spending time with 
you guys, eating tons of good food...

10:54.460 --> 10:56.250
I'm always so happy!

10:56.570 --> 11:01.560
I wanted to spend every day like 
that, even when I get older.

11:02.750 --> 11:06.140
But, you know, I realized that 
wasn't gonna be good enough.

11:07.310 --> 11:10.230
When I watched you and 
Rena-senpai and Tsubasa,

11:11.070 --> 11:14.150
and saw you all working so hard at something,

11:16.110 --> 11:18.070
I thought you were so cool!

11:21.190 --> 11:26.490
But that's totally unfair! 
I want to be cool, too, just like you guys!

11:26.910 --> 11:29.790
That's why I'm going to study makeup!

11:29.790 --> 11:34.450
I'm gonna study and study and one 
day I'll be as cool as you guys are!

11:39.270 --> 11:40.370
You are, huh?

11:40.370 --> 11:41.250
Yeah!

11:42.120 --> 11:42.990
Oh.

11:44.760 --> 11:45.950
It's from Mom.

11:47.050 --> 11:49.710
Oh, crap! I have to get going!

11:49.710 --> 11:51.480
I'll walk you to the car.

11:51.480 --> 11:54.560
That's okay. You're going somewhere 
with your friends, aren't you?

11:54.980 --> 11:56.580
Yeah, well...

11:56.580 --> 11:57.810
Okay, I'm off.

11:57.810 --> 11:58.860
Have a safe trip, okay?

11:59.560 --> 12:00.290
Thanks!

12:13.420 --> 12:17.790
Akino-san

12:14.310 --> 12:17.790
<b><i>I just saw Fuyuki. She's on 
her way to the airport now.</i></b>

12:19.500 --> 12:21.300
<b><i>Aren't you gonna go say goodbye?</i></b>

12:29.330 --> 12:31.680
Okay. You guys ready for some karaoke?

12:31.680 --> 12:34.080
What? I thought you weren't coming.

12:34.080 --> 12:36.480
I can't spend all my time gaming, right?

12:40.520 --> 12:44.400
Hey, Sayu-nee! Wait up, wait up!

12:46.410 --> 12:51.120
To Tsubasa,

I'm so sorry! I did talk to Mom
about this but I still have to go home.
 You looked so tired and were sleeping
so peacefully, I didn't want to wake
you up. Sorry for the trouble

12:46.840 --> 12:51.120
<i>After that night, I didn't 
know how to face Fuyuki-san.</i>

13:03.100 --> 13:05.490
<i>I thought it meant she 
didn't like me anymore.</i>

13:06.510 --> 13:10.440
<i>But if I don't see her now, then...</i>

13:06.930 --> 13:10.850
To Tsubasa,

I'm so sorry! I did talk to Mom
about this but I still have to go home.
 You looked so tired and were sleeping
so peacefully, I didn't want to wake
you up. Sorry for the trouble

13:11.810 --> 13:17.060
<i>I want to see her. I want to see her, 
but my body won't move.</i>

13:17.910 --> 13:22.770
<i>Get over yourself, man! If you don't 
hurry up, her plane is gonna leave!</i>

13:23.330 --> 13:24.990
<i>You might never be able to see her again!</i>

13:31.450 --> 13:32.120
Huh?

13:32.450 --> 13:33.980
This is Fuyuki-san's hairpin.

13:34.420 --> 13:39.090
But why was it in my bag? 
Did it fall in at some point?

13:40.100 --> 13:41.330
I've got to give it back.

13:44.110 --> 13:45.870
<i>Maybe it was just my imagination,</i>

13:46.570 --> 13:48.650
<i>but it felt like she was 
giving me a little push.</i>

13:50.330 --> 13:54.520
<i>That did it. I've got to return 
this before Fuyuki-san goes away.</i>

13:55.220 --> 13:55.810
<i>I'll go.</i>

13:56.920 --> 13:57.800
<i>I'm going!</i>

14:04.320 --> 14:05.980
<i>I'm going to see Fuyuki-san!</i>

14:07.900 --> 14:09.060
Dad!

14:10.820 --> 14:13.800
Wh-What, Tsubasa? D-Don't scare me like that!

14:14.140 --> 14:17.080
I need you to take me to 
Memanbetsu Airport right now!

14:17.400 --> 14:20.110
Hold on. What is this, all of a sudden?

14:20.110 --> 14:21.390
Please, take me!

14:21.390 --> 14:25.340
Sorry, but I can't. I have a 
remote meeting in a few minutes.

14:25.550 --> 14:28.500
What do you need to go to 
Memanbetsu Airport for anyway?

14:28.500 --> 14:31.150
It can't wait! 
I have to go see someone there!

14:31.670 --> 14:32.640
No matter what!

14:36.500 --> 14:37.070
Dad!

14:37.070 --> 14:38.980
Hello. How are things going?

14:38.980 --> 14:41.570
Did you send the materials 
for the meeting already?

14:42.950 --> 14:45.370
Oh, thank you! I'll check them.

14:45.370 --> 14:48.700
And, hate to do this to you, 
but could you handle the meeting for me?

14:49.420 --> 14:53.190
Yeah. Sorry. I'll check everything 
when I'm back in Tokyo.

14:53.190 --> 14:56.070
Yeah. I'll let the other 
team know what's happening.

14:56.930 --> 14:58.310
Okay. Thanks.

14:59.290 --> 15:00.210
Dad...

15:01.250 --> 15:02.530
This is a moment

15:03.010 --> 15:05.050
neither of you want to regret, right?

15:07.140 --> 15:10.600
Let's go, Tsubasa. Hurry and get dressed.

15:10.600 --> 15:11.570
Okay!

15:11.890 --> 15:13.970
Memanbetsu Airport

15:16.010 --> 15:21.670
I'm so excited to go overseas again! 
I'm gonna shop 'til I drop!

15:28.040 --> 15:32.050
D-Don't worry. I'll be there 
on the first day with you.

15:32.050 --> 15:34.920
You don't need to be so nervous, okay?

15:35.330 --> 15:37.290
Oh. Yeah.

15:42.600 --> 15:44.740
It's the 2:10 flight, right?

15:45.060 --> 15:48.100
No problem. At this rate, 
we'll make it in time.

15:48.100 --> 15:49.100
Yeah.

15:48.510 --> 15:51.260
<b>Saturday, May 5</b>

15:49.710 --> 15:50.850
<i>Fuyuki-san...</i>

16:00.920 --> 16:05.190
<i>The 2:10 flight to New Chitose 
Airport will soon be...</i>

16:06.260 --> 16:07.850
That's our flight, isn't it?

16:10.370 --> 16:14.350
I'm gonna run to the bathroom, 
so will you wait for me at the gate?

16:14.350 --> 16:15.700
Oh. Okay.

16:16.760 --> 16:19.650
Yeah. He isn't gonna come.

16:20.930 --> 16:23.550
I guess one little hairpin wasn't enough.

16:26.080 --> 16:27.670
<b>Departure Lounge</b>

16:34.550 --> 16:36.140
Fuyuki-san!

16:38.390 --> 16:39.330
Fuyuki-san!

16:40.140 --> 16:41.320
Fuyuki-san!

16:42.290 --> 16:43.690
Fuyuki-san!

16:45.600 --> 16:47.140
Fuyuki-san!

16:47.610 --> 16:50.010
Tsu... Tsubasa?!

16:52.900 --> 16:56.440
Mii is never this quiet.

16:56.440 --> 16:59.660
She must be really nervous 
about studying abroad.

17:07.290 --> 17:08.460
But why...

17:08.460 --> 17:12.500
Here. I found this inside my bag.

17:14.200 --> 17:16.900
Huh? No way! Thank you!

17:16.900 --> 17:19.860
You came all the way here to give it back?

17:20.230 --> 17:21.050
Yeah.

17:22.470 --> 17:24.250
Also...

17:25.900 --> 17:28.480
I really needed to see you before you left,

17:30.840 --> 17:31.980
Fuyuki-san!

17:34.350 --> 17:37.650
C-Come on! That's so cliché, Tsuba-cha!

17:41.980 --> 17:44.830
I'm so glad that I came to Hokkaido.

17:45.580 --> 17:48.670
And I'm so glad I met you, Fuyuki-san.

17:49.160 --> 17:51.250
At first, I was really nervous.

17:51.670 --> 17:55.800
Coming from Tokyo, I didn't know 
if I could make it by myself here.

17:56.110 --> 18:01.430
But you were always there for me, 
and you made every day fun and interesting.

18:02.290 --> 18:05.220
I was happier than I'd ever been before!

18:05.730 --> 18:09.550
I knew that things would turn around 
for me here. I was sure of it.

18:10.210 --> 18:16.900
And so I... Hokkaido, Kitami... this place 
where I found you... I love all of it!

18:17.750 --> 18:22.760
And six months, or a year from now... 
I don't know how long you'll be gone,

18:22.760 --> 18:23.830
but I'll be waiting for you.

18:24.440 --> 18:27.890
When you come back, let's go 
see the blossoms again, okay?

18:30.890 --> 18:32.950
I-It's two weeks.

18:34.050 --> 18:34.700
Eh?

18:35.800 --> 18:37.170
It's, like, two weeks.

18:38.700 --> 18:41.310
I mean, it's a short-term program.

18:41.310 --> 18:43.150
Eh?!

18:43.620 --> 18:46.110
It's only... two weeks?

18:46.110 --> 18:50.610
Hey, two weeks is still super crazy for me!

18:50.610 --> 18:51.190
Huh?

18:52.390 --> 18:58.770
I've never left Hokkaido before. 
And it's my first trip overseas.

18:59.150 --> 19:02.420
I am excited about it, but I didn't 
think I'd get this nervous.

19:02.920 --> 19:05.730
I think I understand how you felt now.

19:05.730 --> 19:06.790
Fuyuki-san...

19:07.040 --> 19:08.840
But I'll be okay now.

19:09.820 --> 19:14.180
You just wait and see, okay? When I get 
back, I'll totally have caught up to you!

19:14.740 --> 19:17.630
I'm gonna come back super grown up!

19:22.890 --> 19:25.720
Yeah. Have a great trip.

19:25.720 --> 19:27.830
Thanks! I'll see you soon!

19:31.710 --> 19:35.570
It looks like bringing you to 
Hokkaido was the right choice.

19:37.090 --> 19:37.930
Yeah.

19:41.320 --> 19:43.480
Thank you, Dad.

19:44.850 --> 19:48.170
Okay! Why don't we get sushi on the way back?

19:48.170 --> 19:49.000
Really?

19:49.000 --> 19:52.990
Sure! The sushi in Hokkaido is delicious!

21:28.200 --> 21:30.520
Oh, Shiki. Morning!

21:30.520 --> 21:31.560
Morning!

21:32.630 --> 21:33.490
Shiki.

21:34.210 --> 21:35.480
M-Morning.

21:35.710 --> 21:36.930
Morning.

21:36.930 --> 21:42.040
Hey, there's an event this weekend 
when you can pick up a rare item.

21:42.550 --> 21:44.260
Wanna try it together?

21:44.260 --> 21:47.970
Oh, that sounds like fun. Yeah, let's do it!

21:47.970 --> 21:51.820
Really? Ah, but you better 
not hold me back, man.

21:51.820 --> 21:55.960
What? Oh, fine. 
I'll be sure to level up first.

21:55.960 --> 21:56.760
Cool.

21:58.120 --> 22:00.540
What is that? No bento today?

22:00.540 --> 22:04.520
Huh? Oh, yeah. This is something else.

22:07.340 --> 22:09.010
All right. I'll catch you later.

22:09.010 --> 22:09.790
Yeah.

22:10.440 --> 22:12.930
Now then, it's time to take attendance.

22:13.620 --> 22:14.630
Sato-kun?

22:14.630 --> 22:15.460
Here.

22:15.810 --> 22:16.970
Shiki-kun?

22:18.250 --> 22:21.600
Shiki-kun? Is Shiki-kun absent today?

22:21.600 --> 22:23.180
Oh! Here!

22:23.730 --> 22:26.190
Good morning!

22:26.940 --> 22:28.070
What?!

22:31.950 --> 22:34.580
I'm back, Kitami!

22:34.580 --> 22:35.590
Whoa!

22:35.590 --> 22:36.990
Welcome back, Fuyumina!

22:35.950 --> 22:36.990
It's Fuyumina!

22:36.990 --> 22:38.800
We missed you!

22:36.990 --> 22:40.650
Goodness, Fuyuki-san! 
Arriving late on your first day back?

22:38.800 --> 22:40.650
Did you bring us anything?

22:40.650 --> 22:42.490
You certainly haven't changed.

22:44.110 --> 22:46.520
Please hurry up and take 
your seat, all right?

22:46.520 --> 22:51.390
We rotated seats while you were gone, 
so you'll be sitting next to Shiki-kun now.

22:51.390 --> 22:53.890
I'm still taking attendance!

22:53.890 --> 22:57.120
Please, everyone, settle down!

22:57.120 --> 22:58.690
Fuyuki-san. Here.

22:58.690 --> 23:00.810
What, what?

23:01.670 --> 23:04.790
Yay! It's chicken from Seicomart!

23:04.790 --> 23:09.170
Thanks, Tsubasa! I totally 
missed my Seicomart chicken!

23:09.170 --> 23:11.450
I knew you'd want some, Fuyuki-san.

23:11.450 --> 23:12.950
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

23:15.430 --> 23:17.420
It's super delish!

23:18.380 --> 23:19.940
Here. You, too.

23:21.060 --> 23:22.420
Say "ahh!"

23:31.110 --> 23:32.470
You two!

23:32.470 --> 23:37.000
You can't arrive late and then just 
start eating in class, Fuyuki-san!

23:37.000 --> 23:39.540
You, too, Shiki-kun. 
What in the world are you doing?

23:39.540 --> 23:41.750
Uh... I'm very sorry.

23:41.750 --> 23:44.940
I want you both to come and 
see me after class. Okay?

23:45.810 --> 23:47.350
Okay.

23:46.060 --> 23:47.350
Oway.

23:47.350 --> 23:50.290
All right, we're finishing attendance!

23:54.040 --> 23:55.810
I'm back, Tsubasa!

23:56.150 --> 23:58.140
Welcome home, Fuyuki-san!
